id: pm-aiqmgj
title: Native SQLite warnings corrupt strict machine-channel acceptance on Node 24.12
description: "Canonical full coverage on Node 24.12.0 completed 9386 passing tests but failed workflow-policy MCP JSON parsing and lossless mutation stderr cleanliness because native SQLite ExperimentalWarning text preceded application output. Preserve application diagnostics and determine the runtime capability or subprocess boundary responsible, without globally silencing warnings or weakening assertions."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:ci","area:sdk","horizon:current",runtime-compatibility
created_at: "2026-09-28T09:20:34.544Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-08T06:31:09.941Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-08T06:31:09.197Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-08T06:31:09.197Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce the two affected tests on Node 24.12 and compare supported Node 22/current; identify the actual production or harness boundary; preserve unexpected application-warning and JSON assertions; add a negative control and prove focused supported-runtime coverage without global warning suppression
goal: project management = context management
objective: Keep runtime diagnostics from invalidating machine-readable contracts
value: Agents can trust structured refusal and mutation channels across supported runtimes
impact: CLI subprocess and MCP parity validation
outcome: Portable strict machine-channel acceptance
why_now: Discovered during full validation of current SDK mutation contracts
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Both native indexes share an exact synchronous warning filter; direct tests now load the real constructor under that filter and verify a fresh native subprocess without hiding application diagnostics.
expected_result: Native SQLite first loading leaves machine channels clean and normal warning delivery restored; application warnings and original strict CLI assertions remain active.
actual_result: "Node 22 linked native acceptance and all 22 Node 24 focused cases pass, including a real cold in-memory database and visible application diagnostic. All first-head hosted checks and the local static aggregate pass; final updated-head CI and re-review remain required before merge."
